{
  "intro": [
    {
      "text": "A Rosharan nation whose lands once belonged to the Silver Kingdom of Makabakam.",
      "revealedIn": ["way-of-kings"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A kingdom in southwestern Roshar and a member nation of the Azish Empire.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "65" }]
    }
  ],
  "description": [
    {
      "text": "The people of Alm are Makabaki, mostly dark of skin and hair.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "19" },
            { "book": "edgedancer", "chapter": "4" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "fromCulture": "people"
    },
    {
      "text": "Alm and neighbouring Desh have a more countrified air than the other Azish lands, and Alm's clothes are plainer and lighter in colour than its neighbours' fashions.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "19" },
            { "book": "edgedancer", "chapter": "4" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "fromCulture": "dress"
    },
    {
      "text": "Like the other Azish member states, Alm governs itself but recognises the Prime Aqasix as emperor and generally follows Azir's lead abroad.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "65" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "A small nation that borders Yezier and Liafor, with the Misted Mountains standing between it and Shinovar. The bulk of its territory sits between the mountains and a broad river, and it has a short stretch of coast on a bay that opens onto the Aimian Sea.",
      "revealedIn": ["oathbringer"]
    }
  ],
